#           "text": "{\"results\":[{\"description\":\"description: Installs the Agent Framework, Foundry hosting package, Azure Identity, and python-dotenv packages using pip.\\npackage: agent-framework, agent-framework-foundry-hosting, azure-identity, python-dotenv\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"pip install -U agent-framework agent-framework-foundry-hosting azure-identity python-dotenv\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/how-to/develop/framework-hosted-agents?pivots=programming-language-python#install-the-packages\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Defines a CLAUDE.md file for a Microsoft Agent Framework project, providing project overview, tech stack, architecture, commands for running, testing, and deploying the agent, code patterns for using AzureAIAgentClient with AzureCliCredential, and current sprint tasks.\\npackage: agent-framework, Microsoft Foundry, MCP tools, AzureAIAgentClient, AzureCliCredential\\nlanguage: markdown\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"# Project: Customer Service Agent\\r\\n\\r\\n## Overview\\r\\nMulti-agent system using Microsoft Agent Framework with Foundry Agent Service.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tech Stack\\r\\n- Python 3.11\\u002B\\r\\n- agent-framework (Microsoft Agent Framework Python SDK)\\r\\n- Microsoft Foundry for hosted agents\\r\\n- MCP tools for enterprise data access\\r\\n\\r\\n## Architecture\\r\\n- \\u0060src/agents/\\u0060 - Agent definitions (triage, specialist, escalation)\\r\\n- \\u0060src/tools/\\u0060 - MCP tool implementations\\r\\n- \\u0060src/workflows/\\u0060 - Multi-agent orchestration\\r\\n- \\u0060tests/\\u0060 - pytest with async fixtures\\r\\n\\r\\n## Commands\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/foundry-models/how-to/configure-claude-code#create-project-context-with-claudemd\",\"language\":\"markdown\"},{\"description\":\"description: Installs the agent-framework-foundry Python package using pip, which provides support for Microsoft Foundry model provider functionalities.\\npackage: agent-framework-foundry\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"pip install agent-framework-foundry\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/agent-framework/integrations/by-component/model-providers/microsoft-foundry?pivots=programming-language-python#installation\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Installs the Microsoft Agent Framework, Agent Framework Foundry integration, Azure AI Evaluation SDK, pandas, and python-dotenv packages using pip.\\npackage: agent-framework, agent-framework-foundry, azure-ai-evaluation, pandas, python-dotenv\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"pip install agent-framework\\u003E=1.0.0 agent-framework-foundry \\\\\\r\\n        azure-ai-evaluation pandas python-dotenv\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry-classic/how-to/how-to-migrate-prompt-flow-to-agent-framework#prerequisites\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Clones the entire Microsoft Foundry samples repository and navigates to the Python tutorial directory for the enterprise agent idea-to-prototype sample.\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/microsoft-foundry/foundry-samples.git\\r\\ncd foundry-samples/samples/python/enterprise-agent-tutorial/1-idea-to-prototype\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/tutorials/developer-journey-idea-to-prototype#get-the-sample-code\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Initializes a hosted agent from the Foundry toolbox sample using the Azure Developer CLI, scaffolding the agent into a specified source directory and connecting it to a model deployment.\\npackage: azure.ai.agents\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"mkdir my-toolbox-agent \\u0026\\u0026 cd my-toolbox-agent\\r\\nazd ai agent init -m \\u0022https://github.com/microsoft-foundry/foundry-samples/blob/main/samples/python/hosted-agents/agent-framework/responses/04-foundry-toolbox/azure.yaml\\u0022 --src src/toolbox-agent\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/quickstart-toolbox-agent?pivots=csharp#step-1-initialize-the-hosted-agent\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates a new directory for the hosted agent, navigates into it, and initializes a Foundry hosted agent using the Azure Developer CLI with a specified model and source directory.\\npackage: azure.ai.agents\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"mkdir my-toolbox-agent \\u0026\\u0026 cd my-toolbox-agent\\r\\nazd ai agent init -m \\u0022https://github.com/microsoft-foundry/foundry-samples/blob/main/samples/python/hosted-agents/agent-framework/responses/04-foundry-toolbox/azure.yaml\\u0022 --src src/toolbox-agent\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/quickstart-toolbox-agent?pivots=python#step-1-initialize-the-hosted-agent\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates a new directory named \\u0027my-memory-agent\\u0027, navigates into it, and initializes a hosted agent using the Foundry memory sample by running the \\u0027azd ai agent init\\u0027 command with a specified YAML configuration URL. This sets up the sample files and provisioning scripts for the memory store and agent.\\nlanguage: powershell\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"mkdir my-memory-agent\\r\\ncd my-memory-agent\\r\\nazd ai agent init -m \\u0022https://github.com/microsoft-foundry/foundry-samples/blob/main/samples/python/hosted-agents/agent-framework/responses/13-foundry-memory/azure.yaml\\u0022\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/quickstart-memory-hosted-agent?pivots=azd#step-1-initialize-the-hosted-agent\",\"language\":\"powershell\"},{\"description\":\"description: Installs the Foundry Local SDK and OpenAI Python packages for Windows, integrating with Windows ML runtime.\\npackage: foundry-local-sdk-winml, openai\\nlanguage: bash\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"pip install foundry-local-sdk-winml openai\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry-local/get-started?pivots=programming-language-python#install-packages\",\"language\":\"bash\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates a new directory for the Foundry IQ agent, navigates into it, and initializes the hosted agent using the Azure Developer CLI with a specified Foundry IQ sample configuration file.\\nlanguage: powershell\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"mkdir my-foundry-iq-agent\\r\\ncd my-foundry-iq-agent\\r\\nazd ai agent init -m \\u0022https://github.com/microsoft-foundry/foundry-samples/blob/main/samples/python/hosted-agents/agent-framework/responses/17-foundry-iq-toolbox/azure.yaml\\u0022\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/quickstart-foundry-iq-hosted-agent#step-1-initialize-the-hosted-agent\",\"language\":\"powershell\"}]}",
