#           "text": "{\"results\":[{\"description\":\"description: Shows how to instantiate an Agent with FoundryChatClient configured for web search tool and a local custom function tool (get_weather), enabling the agent to use both web search and local code capabilities.\\npackage: agent_framework\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"agent = Agent(\\r\\n    client=FoundryChatClient(\\r\\n        project_endpoint=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT\\u0022],\\r\\n        model=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_MODEL\\u0022],\\r\\n        credential=AzureCliCredential(),\\r\\n    ),\\r\\n    instructions=\\u0022You are a helpful assistant with web and weather capabilities.\\u0022,\\r\\n    tools=[\\r\\n        FoundryChatClient.get_web_search_tool(),\\r\\n        get_weather,  # Local function tool defined with @tool\\r\\n    ],\\r\\n)\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/responses-api?pivots=python#use-the-web-search-tool\",\"language\":\"python\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates an ephemeral agent using FoundryChatClient and Agent class that calls the Responses API on a Foundry project endpoint for model inference and tool orchestration, authenticating with AzureCliCredential.\\npackage: agent_framework, azure.identity\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"import asyncio\\r\\nimport os\\r\\n\\r\\nfrom agent_framework import Agent\\r\\nfrom agent_framework.foundry import FoundryChatClient\\r\\nfrom azure.identity import AzureCliCredential\\r\\n\\r\\nasync def main() -\\u003E None:\\r\\n    agent = Agent(\\r\\n        client=FoundryChatClient(\\r\\n            project_endpoint=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT\\u0022],\\r\\n            model=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_MODEL\\u0022],\\r\\n            credential=AzureCliCredential(),\\r\\n        ),\\r\\n        instructions=\\u0022You are a helpful assistant.\\u0022,\\r\\n    )\\r\\n\\r\\n    result = await agent.run(\\u0022What is the capital of France?\\u0022)\\r\\n    print(f\\u0022Agent: {result}\\u0022)\\r\\n\\r\\nif __name__ == \\u0022__main__\\u0022:\\r\\n    asyncio.run(main())\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/responses-api?pivots=python#create-an-agent\",\"language\":\"python\"},{\"description\":\"description: Defines an asynchronous Python function that creates an ephemeral agent using FoundryChatClient with Azure CLI credentials, configures it with web search tool access, and runs a query to get the latest updates about Microsoft Foundry, printing the result.\\npackage: agent_framework, azure.identity\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"import asyncio\\r\\nimport os\\r\\n\\r\\nfrom agent_framework import Agent\\r\\nfrom agent_framework.foundry import FoundryChatClient\\r\\nfrom azure.identity import AzureCliCredential\\r\\n\\r\\nasync def main() -\\u003E None:\\r\\n    agent = Agent(\\r\\n        client=FoundryChatClient(\\r\\n            project_endpoint=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT\\u0022],\\r\\n            model=os.environ[\\u0022FOUNDRY_MODEL\\u0022],\\r\\n            credential=AzureCliCredential(),\\r\\n        ),\\r\\n        instructions=\\u0022You are a research assistant. Use web search to find current information.\\u0022,\\r\\n        tools=[\\r\\n            FoundryChatClient.get_web_search_tool(),\\r\\n        ],\\r\\n    )\\r\\n\\r\\n    result = await agent.run(\\u0022What are the latest updates to Microsoft Foundry?\\u0022)\\r\\n    print(f\\u0022Agent: {result}\\u0022)\\r\\n\\r\\nif __name__ == \\u0022__main__\\u0022:\\r\\n    asyncio.run(main())\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/agents/quickstarts/responses-api?pivots=python#use-the-web-search-tool\",\"language\":\"python\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates a FoundryChatClient with credentials, endpoint, and model, then creates an Agent instance using this client and instructions, enabling communication with the LLM service through the chat client pipeline.\\npackage: agent_framework, agent_framework.foundry\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"from agent_framework import Agent\\r\\nfrom agent_framework.foundry import FoundryChatClient\\r\\n\\r\\nclient = FoundryChatClient(\\r\\n    credential=credential,\\r\\n    project_endpoint=endpoint,\\r\\n    model=model,\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nagent = Agent(client=client, instructions=\\u0022You are helpful.\\u0022)\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/agent-framework/concepts/agents/agent-pipeline?pivots=programming-language-python#agent-pipeline\",\"language\":\"python\"},{\"description\":\"description: Creates a FoundryChatClient instance with credentials, endpoint, and model, then creates an Agent instance using this client and instructions, enabling communication with an LLM service through the chat client pipeline.\\npackage: agent_framework, agent_framework.foundry\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"from agent_framework import Agent\\r\\nfrom agent_framework.foundry import FoundryChatClient\\r\\n\\r\\nclient = FoundryChatClient(\\r\\n    credential=credential,\\r\\n    project_endpoint=endpoint,\\r\\n    model=model,\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nagent = Agent(client=client, instructions=\\u0022You are helpful.\\u0022)\",\"link\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/agent-framework/concepts/agents/agent-pipeline?pivots=programming-language-python#agent-pipeline\",\"language\":\"python\"},{\"description\":\"description: Defines an asynchronous Python function that creates an ephemeral agent using FoundryChatClient with Azure CLI credentials, sends a prompt to the agent with streaming enabled, and prints the response tokens incrementally as they are received.\\npackage: agent_framework, azure.identity\\nlanguage: python\\n\",\"codeSnippet\":\"import asyncio\\r\\nimport os\\r\\n\\r\\nfrom agent_framework import Agent\\r\\nfrom agent_framework.foundry import FoundryChatClient\\r\\nfrom azure.identity import AzureCliCredential\\r\\n\\r\\nasync def main() -\\u003E None:\\r\\n    